JWasm: -Zj reads the source in every pass and evaluates IF1/IF2 by pass

MASM 5 reads the source again in each pass. JWasm normally saves the
lines of pass one and replays them, which it can't do here: STRUC.INC's
macros generate different code in pass two (IFDEF of labels defined later
in pass one, IF1/IF2), so the lines are not the same. Under -Zj:

- the saved-lines optimisation (fastpass.c) is off, every pass reads the
  source again;
- IF1 is true in pass one only, IF2 in later passes only, as in MASM 5
  (JWasm: IF1 is always true, IF2 an error);
- IFDEF/IFNDEF of a symbol defined in pass one is true in later passes,
  before its definition is reached again (STRUC.INC's forward labels);
- IFDEF/IFNDEF accept the name in angle brackets (ifndef <$ll&l>);
- OPTION NOKEYWORD acts in every pass, and the keywords it disabled are
  enabled again at the end of each pass, so that a line before the OPTION
  (COMMAND1.ASM's NAME, before COMSW.ASM's OPTION NOKEYWORD:<NAME ...>)
  means the same in every pass;
- an EXTRN first seen after pass one (in IF2: COMMAND's INIT.ASM) gets
  an EXTDEF, as MASM 5 writes the object in pass two: the header, written
  after pass one, is written again and the module assembled once more;
- the warning for too many macro arguments is given in pass one only.

